# AGENT.md — src/domain/

The innermost layer. Pure business — depends on nothing.

## What lives here

- `entities/<module>/` — domain entities. Plain TypeScript classes with no
  ORM decorators.
- `repositories/<module>/` — repository interfaces. The domain declares what
  it needs; infrastructure provides the implementation.

## Rules

- **Zero imports from `application/` or `infrastructure/`.**
- **Zero framework imports.** No Express, no NestJS, no ORM decorators.
- Entities are plain classes with explicit constructors.
- Repository interfaces are just TypeScript interfaces — no injection tokens
  needed (Express has no DI container).
